# api: human-edited dependency source.
# Lockfile (`requirements.txt`) is auto-generated from this file by `uv pip compile`.
#
# When adding/upgrading a dependency:
#   1. Edit this file (loose ranges OK for utilities; pin ML/server core).
#   2. Run: uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt --python-version 3.11 --universal
#   3. Verify the new license is OSS-compatible (Apache-2.0 / MIT / BSD / LGPL).
#   4. Commit BOTH files together with a license-confirmation trail in the body:
#        LICENSE: <pkg> <version> <SPDX-id> confirmed at <URL>
#
# ML / server-core packages are pinned to the version family currently
# validated for the cls-studio runtime on Python 3.11. Bumping a major
# version is a deliberate compatibility-test event — re-run pytest + a
# scoring smoke run before relaxing these pins.
#
# NOTE: the torch-family pins here may skew from requirements.in, and the
# reason is the CUDA index, not a preference: this variant is installed on
# Windows from https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130, and only the torch
# versions that index actually builds are reachable here.
#
# This set was on cu128 until 2026-08-17. PyTorch stopped building cu128
# wheels at torch 2.11.0, which stranded a known-vulnerable torch
# (PYSEC-2025-194) and, through torch 2.11's own setuptools<82 requirement,
# a vulnerable setuptools with it. cu130 ships 2.13.0 and covers the same
# architectures cu128 did (sm_75 Turing through sm_120 Blackwell, verified
# with torch.cuda.get_arch_list()). The cost is CUDA 13.x's driver floor:
# >= 580. Older GPUs keep the separate cu124 path in install_windows.bat.
#
# Before changing a pin here, check what the index actually has:
#   https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130/torch/
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md ("Dependency policy") for the full flow.

# ── Core server (pinned to validated minor families) ────────────
fastapi==0.135.*
uvicorn[standard]==0.42.*
sqlmodel==0.0.*
pydantic==2.12.*
python-multipart==0.0.*
httpx==0.28.*

# ── ML / inference (pinned to validated major.minor) ────────────
# torch CUDA suffix (`+cu130`) is environment-specific and intentionally
# absent here — the lockfile records canonical PyPI versions
# (`torch==2.13.0`) and CI installs CPU wheels via --extra-index-url.
torch==2.13.*
numpy==2.4.*
pillow>=10.2.0,<13
opencv-python-headless>=4.9.0,<5
scikit-learn==1.8.*
scipy==1.17.*

# ── Large image tiling (DeepZoom pyramid generation) ────────────

# ── Chunked mask storage for large images ───────────────────────
zarr>=2.18.0,<3

# DINOv2 is fetched at runtime via torch.hub (weights Apache-2.0);
# no extra Python dependency is needed for it beyond torch itself.

# ── OpenVINO export (Intel edge) is opt-in: ~300MB+ of wheels.
# Installed by `install_windows.bat --with-openvino` from
# `requirements-openvino.in` rather than bundled here.

# ── Config loading (.env files) ─────────────────────────────────
python-dotenv>=1.0.0,<2

